{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1206383-specifics-of-plant-mastery","id":1206383,"title":"Specifics of Plant Mastery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-13T05:17:31-07:00","id":1206383,"title":"Specifics of Plant Mastery","content":"So, if I'm a nova and I have the Plant Mastery power (from the <i>Aberrant </i>corebook), how far does that extend? I mean, the text says I can 'talk' to plants and even replicate the 'Animation' power with them, but what can they tell me, and what kinds of things can I talk a plant into doing? Does a tree have any kind of tactile sense or ability to hear what's said under it, or does it just take note of light and dark, when it's watered and when it's not and such? <br /> <br /> Can I become the ultimate topiarist by talking plants into taking weird and wonderful shapes and having them stay like that? If I can and I want to grow oak trees into houses, would it take years or can I talk them into growing at greatly accelerated speeds, provided they have the nutrients and water necessary? Can I ask an apple tree to give me an apple in spring? Can I talk an apple pip into growing into a different species of apple or into a peach or into growing up to have hydrophobic leaves, or is it bound by its genetics?<br /> <br /> Would this depend on how many dots I have in the power? Could/should I develop subsidiary powers ala Elemental Anima's 'Alter Temperature' to allow me to do these things, or are they simply beyond the remit of Plant Mastery - maybe something like 'Chlorokinesis' could do the job instead, a 3rd-level peer of Gravity Control?<br /> <br /> Thoughts and input on this would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-13-2018, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T10:22:49-07:00","id":1206508,"title":"","content":"I think that Plant Mastery is mostly a talk to plants power. So it allows for communication, basic influence and control. <br /> <br /> BUT <br /> <br /> If a player came to m and said I want my nova to have power over the plant world then I would say you need to buy Elemental Anime slash Elemental Mastery but with a plant focus. We would then work together to create or choose techniques for said ability. <br /> <br /> So that in the end said nova could indeed do all that you suggested for them.<br /> <br /> Also some of what your suggatuin might be better developed as a a Super Science project rather than a power use. <br /> <br /> Finally, the idea of a nova creating a species of plan which can grow into massive natural tree houses is in fact an awesome one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T01:18:16-07:00","id":1206816,"title":"","content":"I've made a start on developing a chlorokinetic power. I'm fairly new to Aberrant, so some feedback on the mechanics of the power would be very welcome, as well as other ideas for techniques.<br /> <br /> <b>CHLOROKINESIS</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Level:</b>3<br /> <b>Quantum Minimum:</b> 4<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Special<br /> <b>Range:</b> Special<br /> <b>Area:</b> Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Variable<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The user of this power may control plant life<br /> <b>Multiple Actions:</b> Yes<br /> <b>Description:</b> A nova with this power can control, shape and otherwise manipulate plant life, from causing a flower to bloom in winter to shaping a forest into a living fortress. Novas with this power are highly valued by Project Utopia for its terraforming initiatives and often work in conjunction with nova and baseline biologists to create and cultivate new and marvellous plants via accelerated selective breeding or with the aid of genetic engineering. This power only allows a nova to control plants \u2013 that is, organisms which use chloroplasts to photosynthesize. Algae is within their powers, although fungi and moulds are not. Symbiotic organisms like mosses and lichens which are only partly plants are left to the discretion of the storyteller.<br /> <br /> A nova with this power may spend 1 quantum point and roll Perception + Chlorokinesis to intuitively sense the state, species and properties of a plant within (Quantum + Chlorokinesis) x 20 metres. If the nova has not encounted this plant before, they recognize that this is not a species they know.<br /> <br /> Like Elemental Mastery, Chlorokinesis comes with a number of techniques, one of which can be learned per dot in this power.<br /> <br /> <b>GROW/WITHER</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Charisma + Chlorokinesis<br /> <b>Range:</b> (Quantum + power rating) x 5 metres<br /> <b>Area:</b> Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Maintenance<br /> The nova may cause plants to grow explosively or wither away. This power can affect either a single plant or a volume of plant matter of roughly human size per success on the character\u2019s Charisma + Chlorokinesis roll and can multiply the target\u2019s rate of growth by a factor of ten per success (i.e. one success = 10x, two successes = 100x, three successes = 1000x etc) or reduces its size by 25% per success, causing that part of the plant to brown, wither and die. This plant matter may belong to a single plant or many, and may or may not encompass the whole of a plant\u2019s mass \u2013 it is perfectly possible to grow a single branch of a young sapling to enormous size relative to the rest.<br /> <br /> This technique only grows the plant, it does not cause it or any part of it to mature. Furthermore, this technique does not allow the nova to control the nature of the plant\u2019s growth beyond choosing what to grow, only to enable it. Plants will grow as is most advantageous to them \u2013 usually upwards towards the sun \u2013 unless manipulated to do otherwise by other chlorokinetic techniques or via Plant Mastery. Any growth is permanent, but the nova must maintain the technique to keep growing the plants, using his quantum powers to gather useful molecules from the surroundings to construct new cells.<br /> <br /> <b>SHAPE</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Chlorokinesis<br /> <b>Range:</b> (Quantum + power rating) x 5 metres<br /> <b>Area:</b> Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Maintenance<br /> Reshape a plant (e.g. oak into treehouse) permanently<br /> <br /> <b>ANIMATE</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Chlorokinesis<br /> <b>Range:</b> (Quantum + power rating) x 3 metres<br /> <b>Area: </b>Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Concentration<br /> Animate a plant as per \u2018Animation\u2019 to serve as a minion<br /> <br /> <b>ALTER</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Chlorokinesis<br /> <b>Range:</b> (Quantum + power rating) x 5 metres<br /> <b>Area:</b> Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Concentration<br /> Alter a plant within its genes \u2013 turning them on or off, tricking it re: stimuli, making it beat fruit out of season etc<br /> <br /> <b>READ LIFE</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Perception + Chlorokinesis<br /> <b>Range:</b> (Quantum + power rating) x 10 metres<br /> <b>Area:</b> (Quantum + power rating) x 5 metre radius<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> Understand the properties, interrelations and influences of plants within the radius<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-14-2018, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:38:11-07:00","id":1206894,"title":"","content":"Based on the things Antaeus was supposed to have done in his early T2M days, I'd tend to agree that what they have written for Plant Mastery wasn't enough. As it was you had to splice his powers together from Biomanipulation, Plant Mastery, and Elemental Mastery till you get to the Ecological Supremacy effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:44:27-07:00","id":1206900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1206383-specifics-of-plant-mastery?p=1206894#post1206894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the things Antaeus was supposed to have done in his early T2M days, I'd tend to agree that what they have written for Plant Mastery wasn't enough. As it was you had to splice his powers together from Biomanipulation, Plant Mastery, and Elemental Mastery till you get to the Ecological Supremacy effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I can see the Plant Mastery and Elemental MAstery, but I can't find Biomanipulation anywhere. There's Bio-Mastery in the fanmade companion.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nevermind, I've found it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-14-2018, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}